# Glulxercise (glulxercise.ulx) benchmark script — SQ-1428.
#
# One command per line; blank lines and lines starting with '#' are skipped
# by `cargo run -p lanthorn-gvm --example bench` and must be stripped before
# the same script is fed to glulxe (see README.md for the exact command).
#
# Twenty-seven of glulxercise's self-checking test groups, chosen to be a
# DISPATCH benchmark: arithmetic, branching, call/return, stack and memory
# opcodes, plus the string decoder and the linear/binary search opcodes. Each
# reports "Passed." and leaves the machine as it found it, so the list can be
# looped indefinitely — `script_runs_only_passing_tests` in
# `crates/gvm/examples/bench.rs` asserts exactly that (one "Passed." per line,
# no failures), which is what stops a typo'd name from quietly measuring the
# help text instead of an opcode group.
#
# Deliberately ABSENT, and why:
#   random, nonrandom        — PRNG output is implementation-defined, so the
#                              amount of work done differs between engines
#   undo, multiundo, extundo, undorestart, undomemsize, undoheap
#                            — snapshot the whole VM state; that measures
#                              memcpy and allocator, not dispatch
#   restore, protect, memsize, heap
#                            — mutate save state or resize memory, so a
#                              second lap is not the same benchmark
#   glk, gidispa, iosys*, filter, nullio
#                            — measure the host's Glk layer, which is a null
#                              sink here and a real terminal in glulxe: the
#                              one comparison that would NOT be like for like
#   float*, double*, safari5 — real work, but floating point on the host FPU
#                              says nothing about the interpreter loop
operand
arith
bigmul
comvar
comarith
bitwise
shift
trunc
extend
aload
astore
arraybit
call
callstack
jump
jumpform
compare
stack
gestalt
throw
streamnum
strings
ramstring
search
mzero
mcopy
verify
